# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local dev secrets template for Supabase Heartbeat.
#
# 1. Copy this file to `.dev.vars` (which is git-ignored — NEVER commit it).
# 2. Fill in your targets. Each target = one Supabase project to keep alive.
# 3. For real deploys, do NOT use .dev.vars — set the secret instead:
#       wrangler secret put SUPABASE_TARGETS
#
# SUPABASE_TARGETS is a JSON array. Use single quotes around the whole value so
# the inner double quotes are preserved.
#
# Get the API key from: Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API.
# RECOMMENDED: use the anon / publishable key (the one labeled "anon public").
# keepalive() only does SELECT now() and is granted to anon, so the low-privilege
# key is enough — no need to scatter the service_role (god) key across projects.
# (The service_role key also works if you prefer; both are granted EXECUTE.)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

SUPABASE_TARGETS='[{"name":"my-dev","url":"https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co","apiKey":"YOUR_ANON_OR_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY"}]'
